{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0","id":1192506,"title":"Directive 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-06T20:45:25-08:00","id":1192506,"title":"Directive 2.0","content":"The timeline of Aberrant will be updated for the modern day, so the current socio-political climate will definitely play a part. If that\u2019s true, then that could lead to a major rewrite of the Directive since it is composed of the intelligence orgs of Russia, the U.K., the U.S.A., Japan, and eventually Germany. If we assume that the Moscow Crash will continue to be an event, and take into account that the U.K. has already withdrawn from the E.U. in our time, would the same alliances be likely to form?<br /> <br /> And consider the current leadership behind some of those nations; How likely is an intelligence alliance between the USA and Russia after that whole election meddling suspicion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T22:23:08-08:00","id":1192514,"title":"","content":"Well keep in mind it's 10 years in the future (N-Day is &quot;modern day&quot;, the setting &quot;NOW&quot; is 10 years later) and the geopolitical shifts of the Nova Age in that intervening time would make a lot of things a distant concern.<br /> <br /> I'm sure a lot of people in 1931 couldn't fathom the US government arming and supplying the Soviet Union against anti-Marxist Germans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-07-2018, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T22:31:57-08:00","id":1192515,"title":"","content":"That said, can the Directive just be answerable to the five permanent members of the UN Security Council, specifically? Maybe with the larger EU replacing France in order to include Germany?<br /> <br /> This of course means excluding Japan (not a major global intelligence player), and putting in China (whose exclusion while the other four permanent SC members were involved last edition stuck out like a sore thumb).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T01:08:34-08:00","id":1192551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0#post1192506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How likely is an intelligence alliance between the USA and Russia after that whole election meddling suspicion?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of sounding overly glib, probably not substantially more (or less) likely than Aberrant: Worldwide Phase I having viable presidential candidates in <i>four</i> different political parties.<br /> <br /> All kidding aside, it can be tough to predict how the arrival of people like novas can cause drastic shifts in geopolitical scope. Not saying this would be the case, but if the Directive is just as paranoid about what novas can do in the new edition as in the old, that could be the sort of 'common enemy' that might lead them to bury some hatchets.<br /> <br /> (Also, I'd have to dig through my books, but wasn't Aberrant-setting UK kinda isolationist? I seem to recall them going out of their way to reject a lot of the influence of organizations like Project Utopia that came across as a rejection of a lot of the advances of the Nova Age.)<br /> <br /> That said, I'd expect the Directive to be pretty different in any case, largely because it's practically being built out of a different world and may or may not draw from elements and organizations already established in the Trinity core book (whereas the original Aberrant setting was extrapolated heavily from the real world + the Aeon Society floating around in the background).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T17:04:19-08:00","id":1192854,"title":"","content":"I thought that the new edition had the Novas showing up in the 2020s? That's not ten years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T17:11:24-08:00","id":1192856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192854#post1192854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that the new edition had the Novas showing up in the 2020s? That's not ten years.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The setting &quot;NOW&quot; is set 2028. N-Day is 2018.<br /> <br /> <br /> They just moved everything up 20 years from first edition (N-Day 1998, setting &quot;NOW&quot; 2008)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T17:25:18-08:00","id":1192862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192551#post1192551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of sounding overly glib, probably not substantially more (or less) likely than Aberrant: Worldwide Phase I having viable presidential candidates in <i>four</i> different political parties.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not opposed to that happening again in 2E, but there needs to be a constitutional amendment to change the election process to make that possible.<br /> <br /> Or I could see a three viable candidate scenario, though it\u2019s unlikely, if you follow the plot that Madame Secretary did: the sitting President, though reasonably popular with the political mainstream, is out of step with the base of their own party, and loses renomination to an extremist. The sitting President runs in the general anyway.<br /> <br /> Edit: So basically make Lauren Pendleton a small-l libertarian Republican President. As anti-Nova sentiment surges on the far right, and she holds firm against stricter regulation of Novas, she loses renomination to Mark Anthony Green. Meanwhile the Democratic Party nominates Portman. President Pendleton decides to run in the general as an Independent or a capital-L Libertarian on the gamble that the combined factor of electoral bias toward incumbency + the mainstream of both parties and independents wanting to steer away from the extremes of an anti-Nova or a Nova President, gives her strong shot without official major party backing.<br /> <br /> Drop Bernard Morrison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-07-2018, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:10:46-08:00","id":1192915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192862#post1192862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not opposed to that happening again in 2E, but there needs to be a constitutional amendment to change the election process to make that possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>why would a constituational amendment be necissary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:42:43-08:00","id":1192929,"title":"","content":"I like the split three way idea. <br /> <br /> Also is it really that bad if a nova becomes President? Especially if they never used any mind influencing abilities to get the position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:43:52-08:00","id":1192931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192915#post1192915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> why would a constituational amendment be necissary?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because under the current electoral system it is effectively impossible for more than two political parties to be viable at one time - any additional party just splits votes with the ideologically nearest party strengthening the position of the ideologically further away major party, because it's the party with the largest PLURALITY that wins 100% of a given state's electoral votes in almost every state in a Presidential race.<br /> <br /> Add to this that even if the STATES (not the electorate as a whole, because again, almost every state votes as a bloc) split between more than 2 candidates, so no one wins a majority of electoral votes - that just thows the election to the House of Representatives, where the sitting House members (not any of the newly elected ones, but the House as seated in the year the election happens) vote AGAIN as state blocks.<br /> <br /> This system makes it virtually impossible for a new party to be viable except on the ashes of a collapsed party (as last happened in 1860).<br /> <br /> This is less based on intentional rigging than it is an unintended consequence of the system being designed without the assumption of political parties in mind. The Framers believed state loyalty would be the dominant political identity in the United States. They were wrong. Systems that support numerous parties require an electoral system built around the assumption that political parties will and should exist: a constitutional amendment would be required to replace the Presidential election system with (for example) a national popular vote with ranked preference, which favors compromise candidates that people across the spectrum rank as second or third choices. OR a more parliamentary-style system with a proportional distribution of electors (assuming we didn't go as far as to combine the executive and legislative branches as in most Parliamentary countries) based on the national vote, where they must form a majority block to elect a President (this system, as opposed to the ranked system, strengthens the political wings, and gives small parties huge leverage over the major parties to make them give them concessions to help them form majority blocks - you can see this phenomena at play in Israel, or even with the influence of DUP over the Conservative Party in the UK currently, where the Conservatives losing seats to the left, resulted in the strengthening of a MORE RIGHT-WING party because the Conservatives needed said party to stay in power). OR a run-off system, where there's a national vote in November, and if there isn't a majority winner of the popular vote, there's a run-off between the top-two vote getters in December (France uses this system). This will still favor the major parties, but allow the smaller parties to build up resources and potentially be major players, since voting for them in November isn't a direct threat that helps the opposite extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-07-2018, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:46:18-08:00","id":1192932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192929#post1192929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the split three way idea.<br /> <br /> Also is it really that bad if a nova becomes President? Especially if they never used any mind influencing abilities to get the position.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the question the scenario posed. Can you KNOW he isn't using mind influencing powers? What counts as mind influencing? Can there be said to even be an electoral democracy if the would be governing-class can influence elections just by having superhuman Presence or Manipulation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:33:14-08:00","id":1193170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1192506-directive-2-0?p=1192932#post1192932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the question the scenario posed. Can you KNOW he isn't using mind influencing powers? What counts as mind influencing? Can there be said to even be an electoral democracy if the would be governing-class can influence elections just by having superhuman Presence or Manipulation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually an interesting question, but it's the same question that can be asked right now of vanilla humans. When the governing-class can influence elections with money, power, and influence, removing the viability of the public vote (as they just did recently), can it really be said to be an electoral democracy?<br /> <br /> The Directive in 1E seemed to grudgingly accept Portman as POTUS, but they mostly had problems because he was pro-Utopia. One might be tempted to think that if their nova president wasn't pro-Utopia they'd have a different outlook. Their Rus-con elements were apparently perfectly happy to have Sierka be the actual power, even though there was a baseline &quot;president&quot;. Besides, I'd think that finding ways to seal novas out of ruling positions, even if they're suspicious of mega-social meddling or mind-control, would quickly build resentment for the same reasons the Teragen Primacy formed (i.e. you'll have us clean up your messes, fix your socio-economic problems,etc, but you won;t allow us to actually BE in charge even if we WANT to help? wtf?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:50:03-08:00","id":1193317,"title":"","content":"I think that the difficulty of a seeding this question is why it's so worthy of a campaign saga. Hehe <br /> <br /> In some ways I like the way the Aes Sedai of the Second Age of the Wheel of Time saga was organized. They didn't rule over mundane exactly but mundane society didn't really rule over them either. Rather both worked together to benefit all lives, just in different way. <br /> <br /> Am in all this is an intriguing question and I look forward to seeing how it's answered in various continuum universes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}